ingredient_count: 11
---

Boil the @fusilli pasta{350%grams} according the packet instruction in salted boiling @water{2%litres} with @salt{30%ml} until al dente. This should take no more than ~{8-9%minutes}.

While the pasta is boiling, melt the @cold butter{30%ml} in a #pot over low medium heat and lightly saute the @garlic{15%ml}(finely crushed) until it is fragrant but not browned or burnt as this will make the sauce bitter. This will take ~{2-3%minutes}.

Add the @fresh cream{750%ml} and allow the cream to simmer for an additional ~{5%mins} on medium heat, while stirring continuously to ensure the butter and cream amalgamate into a smooth sauce.

Once the cream is lightly bubbling, add @grated cheese{250%grams} and stir for ~{5%mins} until the cheese in thoroughly melted into the cream.

At this point the mixture will be steaming. Now, add the @pasta spice{15%ml}, @salt{5%ml}(to taste), @freshly ground black pepper{1.25%ml} and half the @fresh parsley{15%ml}(chopped, for garnish).

Allow the sauce to cook through for ~{5-7%mins} on low-medium heat and stir continuously until the sauce comes to a slight boil.

Reduce the heat, add the pasta and mix thoroughly. The sauce should now be thick luscious consistency and coat the pasta completely.

If you have reduced the sauce too much add the @?full fat milk{60%ml} to thin the consistency.

Serve and garnish with the remaining parsley.